  "reason": "Evidence: We have only one data point (config_001: rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000 → 48.5% acc), which is a weak baseline. The most critical uncertainty in a multimodal cellular profiling study is whether the image modality carries useful predictive signal at all. Question: config_010 (image_only, singleprofile, resnet50) is a clean single-variable comparison against config_001 that isolates the contribution of the image modality. Why this is the best next experiment: If image_only substantially outperforms or matches RNA-only, multimodal fusion becomes a high-priority direction and we can invest remaining budget there. If image_only is much worse, we know to focus on RNA encoder improvements (scvi, scgpt) and multiprofile aggregation instead. This single experiment resolves the highest-impact design uncertainty before committing budget to the 36 multimodal configurations, and it changes only the model setting (rna→image) while holding profile and architecture simple, making the comparison interpretable."
}

